            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThis kind of customization is usually better to be left to the user who can implement this behavior using autocommands and dedicated events.\r\n\r\nHere is one way of opening Starter buffer when entering new tabpage:\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.starter').setup()\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('TabNewEntered', { callback = function() MiniStarter.open() end })\r\n```\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
